  "id": "interocular-transfer",
  "term": "interocular transfer",
  "definition": "Interocular transfer is the carryover of an aftereffect from one eye to the other after stimulation is shown to only one eye. Comparing whether an effect stays in the same eye or transfers across eyes can be used to infer whether it depends on earlier monocular processing or later binocular processing.",
